# The kernel's review (roadmap os-server.md P15), finding 1: a segment's retype, resumed after another thread's revoke
# gave its untyped's memory back and retyped it, ends KE_STATE, writing
# nothing more (before: KE_OK, a segment over the new space). tests/programs/
# additions.asm, TEST_RV_RETYPE; Bochs, whose timing the races need.
program: additions
define: TEST_CAPS
define: TEST_RV_RETYPE
emulators: bochs
match: contains
timeout: 60
---
additions: B found D inside its retype: 1
additions: D: its 64 KB segment's retype, resumed (KE_STATE expected: 6): 6
additions: done
